I FINDINGS -- 0 warnings, 6 notes
I   note tp-wire-lossy: --tp-wire wht6: all-reduce messages from 128 KiB up carry a quantised payload
I        why: faster prefill, but the model does not compute the exact function; two runs on different world sizes are not comparable token for token
I        fix: --tp-wire exact when exactness matters more than prefill speed
I   note experts-from-host: 11.97 GiB of weights a rank live in the pinned host pool and cross PCIe when they are used
I        why: a prefill step streams every routed layer's pooled experts onto the card, so its speed is bounded by the link; decode reads the ones it routes to
I        fix: more VRAM for the experts: a shorter --max-model-len or fewer --max-num-seqs, --embedding-placement ram, --kv-cache-dtype fp8, or more cards (--tp)
I   note link-capped: card 0000:63:00.0 (rank 0): the card's link is 32.0 GT/s x16 at most, and 0000:60:01.1 above it is 16.0 GT/s x16 at most
I        why: the host side of the link bounds what the card can move to and from host memory: streamed experts, the host pool and the all-reduce when it goes through host memory
I        fix: a slot with the card's full width and speed (the board manual says which slots share lanes), or no riser; nothing to do if the board has no faster slot
I   note link-capped: card 0000:43:00.0 (rank 1): the card's link is 32.0 GT/s x16 at most, and 0000:40:01.1 above it is 16.0 GT/s x16 at most
